Wait for MCI audio drain independently of the movie QPC/output clock.

Wine MCIAVI_player uses Sleep(100) between completed-header checks. Native
NtDelayExecution establishes a relative OS wait; it does not use the movie
QPC counter. The port instead measured each retry through the movie
clock, coupling drain to clock stalls/rate changes and millisecond rounding.

Use an independent 100-ms timer: native CLOCK_MONOTONIC timespec deadlines and
browser real setTimeout callbacks. Cancel outstanding waits on finish/close
and before a new play. Keep the immediate first check and reset-before-notify
ordering. No PCM is added, removed or fitted to an original tail.

This fixes the timer contract, not whole audio/video parity. Device completion
publication and browser output-position accuracy remain separate contracts.

Primary sources:
https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/wine-10.0/dlls/mciavi32/mciavi.c
https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/wine-10.0/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c

